"""Measured GPU transport progress, retaining the failing grazing oracle."""
def apply(sections,sources,source,section,table,cite):
 source('S89','Vulkan core shaderInt64 feature','https://docs.vulkan.org/refpages/latest/refpages/source/VkPhysicalDeviceFeatures.html','Int64 SPIR-V arithmetic requires the shaderInt64 device feature. Basix first validation caught its omission; preparation patch6 adds a separately requested, queried/checked pre-device enable for the PT RNG. Default non-PT targets do not require it.',rights='Official specification linked with original summary; specification prose CC-BY-4.0.')
 source('S90','Basix GPU sampling: retained partial result','https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/docs/sampling-results.json','4096 cases include4095 strict validity comparisons and one explicit exact-horizon classification. Directions/validity and evaluation at actual returned directions pass. The original same-variates sample oracle still fails18 cases; maximum transport-weight difference15.688%. Strict mode rejects it; no-op output is rejected.',kind='local measured partial / failure evidence',rights='Original Basix code and selected numeric receipts MIT.')
 source('S91','Basix progressive Vulkan PT acceptance','https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/docs/progressive-results.json','Eleven-case harness:seven fixed-scene variants with matched24-bit CPU streams and four expected rejections. Ordinary triangle BLAS/TLAS and ray queries; primary hits, ordered accumulation and reset checks. Worst scoped global nRMSE0.0000529705 and low-radiance nRMSE0.00023302. Larger256x256 preview is separately marked as having no CPU image comparison.',kind='local measured scoped correctness',rights='Original Basix code, fixture and image MIT; no vendor implementation or game asset copied.')
 by={s['id']:s for s in sections}
 body=by['reference-renderer']['body']
 body=body.replace('GPU progressive PT, scene import, textures and temporal guides remain pending.','A scoped Vulkan progressive PT now runs; grazing sampling robustness, scene import, textures and temporal guides remain open.')
 body=body.replace('the CPU renderer is the independent reference for that future GPU path.','the CPU renderer remains the independent transport reference.')
 body=body.replace('GPU sampling is not yet tested.','Later sampling checks are measured separately below and remain partial at extreme grazing angles.')
 body=body.replace('<strong>Next gate:</strong> implement GPU material sampling and a small Vulkan ray-query progressive integrator against this reference, then import and depth/motion conventions.','<strong>Current next gate:</strong> resolve grazing sampling conditioning and independently validate GPU distributions/energy, then add import and depth/motion conventions.')
 body+='''<h3>Actual Vulkan progressive transport · scoped scene gate passes</h3>
<figure><img src="assets/progressive-cornell.png" width="256" height="256" alt="Actual Vulkan path-traced original box scene with diffuse and rough-metal boxes"><figcaption>GPU output:256×256,256SPP,depth8. No CPU image comparison was run at this preview resolution; its error fields are null. CPU image comparisons use the smaller acceptance fixtures below. This is not a real-time or UE-detail benchmark.</figcaption></figure>
<p>The renderer builds ordinary triangle BLAS/TLAS on the NoGraphicsAPI-owned Vulkan device, allocates material/scene/output data through a NoGraphicsAPI mapped heap, and uses its command pools and timelines. An explicit native ray adapter binds a conventional AS descriptor and an8-byte pointer root. This is native Vulkan integration, rather than an RT entry point supplied by upstream NoGraphicsAPI.</p>
<p>Original float shaders implement area-light NEE, complementary power MIS, compensated RR and ordered progressive accumulation. CPU/GPU share the tested material formulas and an explicitly selected24-bit uniform stream; the CPU remains double precision. The original CPU53-bit default and its prior image hashes are preserved. CPU reference tests now total76 checks.</p>
<p>The11-case harness includes seven CPU comparisons:32×32/1024SPP, a second seed, one scattering event, NEE without MIS, pure BSDF sampling, no RR and the unsplit light. The default light is split into unequal-area triangles so uniform-triangle selection cannot accidentally pass an area-PMF test.2,560 primary rays match independent CPU intersections; shared-edge index ties require actual proximity to the common edge. GPU batch1 versus batch8 and reset after previous accumulation are identical.</p>
<p>Worst measured global normalized RMSE is0.0000529705 and maximum channel-mean relative error0.0000209903. The low-radiance subset (CPU luminance below2, not an emitter mask) has worst normalized RMSE0.00023302. Declared limits are0.05 global,0.10 low-radiance and0.02 channel-mean relative error. HDR outputs are independently decoded and finite/nonnegative. Omitting PT dispatch, invalid accumulation epoch, zero width and a missing shader are rejected. Full-process core/SyncVal logs are clean, including teardown.</p>'''+cite('S91')+'''
<h3>Sampling numerical gate · partial, with the original failure retained</h3>
<div class="callout"><strong>18 extreme grazing cases remain outside paired transport acceptance</strong><p>Sample directions agree within0.000000962, but reconstructing the half vector from nearly cancelling outgoing and incoming directions amplifies float rounding. The original same-variates CPU/GPU f/PDF comparison still fails18 of4,096 cases. Maximum importance-weight difference is15.688%; this is a local extreme-case result, not whole-image error.</p></div>
<p>A separately named diagnostic verifies direction/validity and the returned f/PDF tuple against CPU evaluation at that exact returned float direction. Those narrower contracts pass; they do not erase the original failure or prove unbiased GPU transport. The original tolerances and model are unchanged. <code>--require-paired-transport</code> still exits unsuccessfully, and an isolated no-op shader fails all4,096 cases. The sampling receipt remains <strong>partial</strong>.</p>
<p>Accordingly, M2-gpu remains partial despite the fixed-scene result. Robust grazing arithmetic and independent GPU sampling-distribution/energy checks are next. Unit-scale float ray offsets and endpoint margins also need thin-gap/large-coordinate acceptance. Only one identity TLAS instance is covered. Import, textures, motion guides, dynamic DLSS, advanced extensions and cross-device performance remain open.</p>'''+cite('S90','S91')+'''
<p><strong>Validation lesson:</strong> the first PT shader declared Int64 for its RNG while the device had not enabled shaderInt64. The pipeline could run on this hardware while validation correctly rejected its contract. Patch6 now queries support and explicitly enables that optional requirement before device creation; non-PT defaults remain unchanged.</p>'''+cite('S89')+'''
<p><a href="sampling-results.json">Partial sampling receipt</a> · <a href="progressive-results.json">Scoped scene harness and preview receipts</a> · <a href="https://github.com/BasixMaster/Basix_Engine/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION.md">Reproduction and numerical limits</a></p>'''
 by['reference-renderer']['body']=body
 by['summary']['body']+='<p><strong>GPU transport progress:</strong> the ordinary Vulkan progressive scene gate passes; M2 remains partial because18 extreme grazing sampling cases still fail the original paired criterion. <a href="#reference-renderer">Actual image, results and retained failure</a>.</p>'+cite('S90','S91')
 by['lessons']['body']+='<p><strong>Two numerical questions:</strong> agreement at the returned float direction can pass while the same-variates double sample gives a different PDF or importance weight. Keep both tests visible. A successful fixed-scene image comparison cannot certify the grazing tail, sampling distribution or general renderer quality.</p>'+cite('S90','S91')

def enrich_library(library):
 library['summary'].append('Scoped progressive Vulkan PT passes11 cases; GPU sampling remains partial with18 retained grazing failures and maximum paired transport-weight discrepancy15.688%.')
 library['findings'].append(dict(id='F19',title='Scoped GPU scene correctness does not close the grazing material gate',question_ids=['Q2'],topic='rendering',claim='Seven ordinary Vulkan PT scene variants agree with the CPU24 reference and four rejection controls pass. Separately,18 extreme grazing same-variates material samples fail and remain visible in strict mode.',evidence_type='measured partial with retained failure',confidence='high',context='2026-10-28 Windows RTX4090/NVIDIA617.42; pinned Slang/Vulkan/validation and preparation patch6.',strengths='Independent primary/CPU image oracles, unequal light areas, explicit variant settings, poisoned output, batch/reset identity, retained strict failure and full-process validation.',limitations='Fixed unit-scale scene only; no independent GPU distribution/energy, robust thin gaps, import/textures/motion, dynamic DLSS or performance comparison.',implications='Keep M2-gpu partial; investigate stable grazing sampling arithmetic and independent distribution/energy checks before broader temporal integration.',tags=['Vulkan','reference PT','numerical conditioning','GPU sampling','roadmap'],evidence=[dict(source_id=s,locator='Receipt metrics, cases and explicit limits',relation='supports',note='Scoped scene pass and material failure are separate claims.') for s in ['S90','S91']]))
 library['actions'][0].update(title='Resolve grazing transport and add renderer guides',finding_ids=['F19'],rationale='A scoped Vulkan progressive scene now runs, but18 grazing samples remain outside the original paired material criterion.',success_criterion='Retained sampling criterion passes a justified numerical implementation plus independent GPU distribution/energy tests; then import/depth/motion/reset clips pass.')
 library['scope_changes'].append('Added actual Vulkan progressive transport and11-case scene harness while retaining the18-case grazing failure as a partial implementation gate. CPU53 default preserved; optional24-bit matched stream and checked shaderInt64 requirement added.')
